Here is a thorough report of the project and all findings.

---

## 1. Overall Project Structure

**Location:** `E:\kaifa\英雄排行\MOBA游戏梯度`

This is a **pure static HTML/CSS/JS** project (zero build tools, zero frameworks, zero external dependencies) that serves as a MOBA hero tier-list dashboard. It supports two games: League of Legends Mobile (LoLM) and Dawn Heroes (曙光英雄).

### File Tree

```
MOBA游戏梯度/
├── index.html                 # Main entry point - game selector + render shell
├── editor.html                # JSON data editor (table editor for raw data files)
├── README.md                  # Project documentation
├── 原任务记录.md               # Historical task notes (algorithm design)
├── css/
│   └── tier-list.css          # Shared styles (dark theme, responsive)
├── js/
│   └── tierlist.js            # Core engine (algorithm + rendering + search + sorting)
├── lolm/
│   ├── config.json            # LoLM configuration (lanes, algorithm params, column defs)
│   ├── 上路.json               # Top lane hero data
│   ├── 打野.json               # Jungle hero data
│   ├── 中路.json               # Mid lane hero data
│   ├── 下路.json               # ADC (bot) hero data
│   ├── 辅助.json               # Support hero data
│   └── HeadIcon/              # ~100 hero avatar PNG images
├── 曙光英雄/
│   ├── config.json            # Dawn Heroes configuration (no lanes, weighted-sum algorithm)
│   ├── 曙光英雄.json           # All-hero data
│   ├── 曙光英雄 copy.json      # Backup copy of hero data
│   ├── analyze.js             # Data validation/analysis script
│   └── HeadIcon/              # ~100 hero avatar PNG images
```

### Technology Stack

- **Pure vanilla JS** -- no React, Vue, Angular, Node, or build steps
- **Dark theme** -- GitHub-dark inspired CSS
- **Responsive** -- 768px breakpoint
- **Client-side computation** -- all tier-list algorithms run in the browser

### Two Main Apps

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `index.html` | Public-facing tier-list dashboard with list/table views, search, sort, lane navigation |
| `editor.html` | Internal admin tool for editing raw JSON data files (the one with paste/clipboard/save logic) |

---

## 2. ALL Code Related to "Paste" (粘贴) Functionality

All paste-related code is in **`E:\kaifa\英雄排行\MOBA游戏梯度\editor.html`**. There are **two distinct paste mechanisms**:

### A. Direct Ctrl+V Paste (Primary mechanism)

**File:** `E:\kaifa\英雄排行\MOBA游戏梯度\editor.html`, lines 870-925

This is a `document.addEventListener('paste', ...)` handler that intercepts clipboard paste events. The key flow:

**Lines 870-872 -- Listener attachment:**
```javascript
console.log('%c[INIT] %cPaste listener attached to document', 'color:#3fb950;font-weight:bold', '');
document.addEventListener('paste', function (e) {
```

**Lines 873-880 -- Determine if paste target is an editable input:**
```javascript
let input = null;
if (e.target.tagName === 'INPUT' && e.target.dataset.col) {
  input = e.target;
} else if (document.activeElement && document.activeElement.tagName === 'INPUT' && document.activeElement.dataset.col) {
  input = document.activeElement;
}
if (!input) return; // not pasting into our editable cell
```

**Lines 883-893 -- Extract clipboard text and decide single vs. multi-line:**
```javascript
const pasteText = (e.clipboardData || window.clipboardData).getData('text');
if (!pasteText) return;
const rawLines = pasteText.replace(/\r\n/g, '\n').replace(/\r/g, '\n').split('\n');
while (rawLines.length && rawLines[rawLines.length - 1].trim() === '') rawLines.pop();
// If only one line, let the default paste behavior handle it (single value)
if (rawLines.length <= 1) return;
```

**Lines 895-925 -- Multi-value paste logic (fill same column, successive rows):**
```javascript
e.preventDefault();
const col = input.dataset.col;
const sortedIdx = parseInt(input.dataset.sortedIdx);
const colInputs = [...$('tableBody').querySelectorAll('input[data-col="' + esc(col) + '"]')]
  .sort((a, b) => parseInt(a.dataset.sortedIdx) - parseInt(b.dataset.sortedIdx));

let filled = 0;
for (let i = 0; i < rawLines.length; i++) {
  const val = rawLines[i].trim();
  if (val === '') continue;
  const target = colInputs[sortedIdx + i];
  if (!target) break; // no more rows in this column
  target.value = val;
  target.dataset.original = val; // mark as "not dirty"
  filled++;
}
// Mark all filled cells as needing save
for (let i = 0; i < filled; i++) {
  const target = colInputs[sortedIdx + i];
  if (target) { const td = target.closest('td'); if (td) td.classList.add('modified'); }
}
updateSaveState();
toast(`已填入 ${filled} 个值到 "${col}" 列，点击「✏️ 应用修改」保存`);
```

### B. Paste Column Button (Fallback modal approach)

**Button definition -- line 378-379:**
```html
<button onclick="showPasteModal()" disabled id="pasteBtn" title="从 Excel 粘贴列数据（兜底方案，优先直接用 Ctrl+V 粘贴）">📋 粘贴列</button>
```

**Function -- lines 927-975 (`showPasteModal`):**
```javascript
function showPasteModal() {
  if (!data) { alert('请先加载数据'); return; }
  const col = prompt('请输入目标列名（当前列: ' + columns.join(', ') + '）', columns[0]);
  if (!col || !columns.includes(col)) { if (col) alert('列名 "' + col + '" 不存在'); return; }
  const text = prompt('请粘贴从 Excel 复制的列数据（每行一个值）：');
  if (!text) return;
  // ... splits lines, auto-detects numbers, writes directly to data[row][col],
  // ... auto-creates new rows if pasted values exceed existing row count,
  // ... recalculates computed fields, re-renders
  toast(`已粘贴 ${values.length} 个值到 "${col}" 列`);
}
```

This modal approach **directly modifies `data` objects** (line 962: `data[i][col] = values[i]`) and then calls `render()`. It is a **fallback** for cases where the clipboard API is blocked. It also auto-creates rows (lines 964-970) if the pasted data has more values than existing rows.

### C. Paste Button Enable/Disable States

**Lines 472, 482** -- The button is disabled when no data is loaded, enabled when data exists:
```javascript
// line 472 (render function, no-data path):
$('pasteBtn').disabled = true;
// line 482 (render function, has-data path):
$('pasteBtn').disabled = false;
```

---

## 3. Code Related to Sorting, Column Selection, and Cell Editing

### A. Sorting (排序)

Sorting occurs in **`editor.html`** (the data editor) and **`js/tierlist.js`** (the public dashboard).

#### editor.html sorting:

**Sort state -- lines 412-413:**
```javascript
let sortKey = null;
let sortDir = 1;  // 1 = asc, -1 = desc
```

**`sortBy()` function -- lines 663-673:** Toggles sort direction or changes sort column. Guards against unsaved changes with a confirm dialog.
```javascript
function sortBy(col) {
  if (hasUnsavedChanges()) {
    if (!confirm('有未保存的修改，排序会导致编辑内容丢失。确定继续排序？')) return;
  }
  if (sortKey === col) { sortDir *= -1; }
  else { sortKey = col; sortDir = 1; }
  render();
}
```

**`getSortedData()` -- lines 649-661:** Returns a sorted copy of `data` using numeric comparison when possible, falling back to Chinese locale string comparison:
```javascript
function getSortedData() {
  if (!data) return [];
  let sorted = [...data];
  if (sortKey && columns.includes(sortKey)) {
    sorted.sort((a, b) => {
      let va = a[sortKey], vb = b[sortKey];
      let na = parseFloat(va), nb = parseFloat(vb);
      if (!isNaN(na) && !isNaN(nb)) return (na - nb) * sortDir;
      return String(va ?? '').localeCompare(String(vb ?? ''), 'zh-CN') * sortDir;
    });
  }
  return sorted;
}
```

**Table header rendering with sort indicators -- lines 502-508:**
```javascript
columns.forEach(col => {
  let cls = '';
  if (sortKey === col) cls = sortDir === 1 ? 'sort-asc' : 'sort-desc';
  if (computedFields[col]) cls += ' col-computed';
  const label = computedFields[col] ? col + ' 🔒' : col;
  headHtml += `<th class="${cls}" onclick="sortBy('${esc(col)}')">${label}
    <span class="sort-arrow">${sortKey === col ? (sortDir === 1 ? '▲' : '▼') : ''}</span></th>`;
});
```

#### tierlist.js sorting:

**`sortTable()` -- lines 703-758:** Client-side DOM sorting of already-rendered table rows. Includes special handling for tier ordering and numeric/string comparison:
```javascript
function sortTable(th, colIdx) {
  const table = th.closest("table");
  const tbody = table.querySelector("tbody");
  const rows = Array.from(tbody.querySelectorAll("tr"));
  const isDesc = th.classList.contains("sorted") && !th.classList.contains("desc");
  // ... determines heroes list, builds column defs
  rows.sort((a, b) => {
    // ... tier-aware, numeric, or string comparison
  });
  rows.forEach(r => tbody.appendChild(r));
}
```

### B. Column Detection (列选择/检测)

**`detectColumns()` -- editor.html lines 437-442:** Auto-discovers all column keys from the JSON data by scanning all object keys:
```javascript
function detectColumns(arr) {
  if (!arr || !arr.length) return [];
  const keys = new Set();
  arr.forEach(obj => Object.keys(obj).forEach(k => keys.add(k)));
  return Array.from(keys);
}
```

There is **no manual column selection UI** in the editor -- all columns found in the data are displayed. The column list is built at line 487: `columns = detectColumns(data);` and used throughout the rendering and sorting logic.

Column definitions (labels, types, formatting) for the public dashboard are configured in **`lolm/config.json`** and **`曙光英雄/config.json`** under the `columns`, `globalColumns`, and `statCards` keys.

### C. Cell Editing

All cell editing logic is in **`editor.html`**:

- **Line 531:** Editable cells render as `<input>` elements with `oninput="markDirty(this)"` and `onfocus="this.select()"`.
- **Line 569-573 (`markDirty`):** Adds a `modified` CSS class (shows an orange dot via `::after` pseudo-element on line 258-267) when the user types.
- **Lines 831-834:** Click on an editable `<td>` focuses its `<input>`.
- **Lines 837-868:** Keyboard navigation -- Tab/Shift+Tab moves between editable cells (line 838-851); Enter without Shift moves down to the same column's next row (lines 853-867).
